-- title:
--   Hensel sections of formally étale A[T]-algebras, non-noetherian base
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a henselian local ring with residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` and residue map `residue A`, let $S$ be a local ring, and let $\varphi \colon A[X] \to S$ be a ring homomorphism which is both formally smooth and formally unramified. Suppose $S$ is, as a ring, a localisation: there are a finitely presented $A$-algebra $P$ and a submonoid $M \subseteq P$ with $S$ an $P$-algebra making $S$ the localisation of $P$ at $M$, and the structure maps are compatible with $\varphi$ on constants, i.e. the image of $a \in A$ in $S$ through $P$ equals $\varphi(C\,a)$ for all $a$. Suppose further given a ring homomorphism $\chi_0 \colon S \to \kappa$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $S$, satisfying $\chi_0(\varphi(C\,a)) = \operatorname{residue}_A(a)$ for all $a \in A$ and $\chi_0(\varphi(X)) = 0$. The conclusion has two parts. First, for every $c \in A$ with $\operatorname{residue}_A(c) = 0$, i.e. $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, there is exactly one ring homomorphism $\chi \colon S \to A$ such that $\chi(\varphi(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a \in A$, such that $\operatorname{residue}_A(\chi(f)) = \chi_0(f)$ for all $f \in S$, and such that $\chi(\varphi(X)) = c$. Second, every ring homomorphism $\chi \colon S \to A$ satisfying the first two of these conditions (with no condition imposed on the value $\chi(\varphi(X))$) has kernel the principal ideal generated by $\varphi(X) - \varphi\bigl(C\,(\chi(\varphi(X)))\bigr)$.
--
--   This is Hensel's lemma for sections of an étale algebra in one variable over a henselian local base, in the form of EGA IV 18.5.17, but with the base not assumed noetherian: instead $S$ is required to be a localisation of a finitely presented $A$-algebra, which is what makes the kernel of a section finitely generated. It is used in the construction of smooth points with their local parameters on a proper algebraic curve over a local ring, via [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_smoothPointPackage_localRing_of_mem_smoothLocus_of_isProper`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_smoothPointPackage_localRing_of_mem_smoothLocus_of_isProper), and it rests on the lifting statement [`HenselianLocalRing.exists_algHom_lift_of_isSmoothAt`](thm.html#HenselianLocalRing.exists_algHom_lift_of_isSmoothAt) for algebras smooth at a prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HenselianLocalRing_existsUnique_section_and_ker_eq_span_of_formallyUnramified_of_isLocalization.lean

import Mathlib

